cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use exchange-lab in teaching or research, cite the tagged release you used,
  not main. A result here can be reproduced only against a fixed version: a run
  directory records the commit it was made with, and `make reproduce` compares
  every file it wrote.
type: software
title: exchange-lab
abstract: >-
  A price-time-priority exchange matching engine in C++20 and a deterministic
  market simulator built on it, for teaching and researching trading strategies:
  paired experiments, tested controls and byte-for-byte reproduction. The market
  is invented, so what a strategy earns in it predicts nothing about a real venue.
authors:
  - given-names: Philbert
    family-names: Poku
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/PhillysTheBest/exchange-lab
keywords:
  - market microstructure
  - matching engine
  - limit order book
  - market simulation
  - trading strategies
  - reproducibility
